otengine/godot/pull/105959.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Now that #96169 is merged, adding keywords to classes can help new users discover nodes and resources more easily. My changes can be categorized like so:\r\n\r\n- A class serves multiple purposes, but its name only represents one.\r\n  - XR should alias to VR (arguably also AR, but it's likely not as common). Hope it's not too much of a maintenance burden, having to remember to add this to new XR* classes.\r\n  - CheckBox is also used for radio buttons (!)\r\n- A class uses unconventional abbreviations in its name.\r\n  - H/V for horizontal/vertical were the biggest offenders in terms of discoverability.\r\n- For the remaining classes, I tried thinking about what users who don't know the engine would try searching for.\r\n\r\nI did not dig too deep into *every class* of Godot, especially since many of them would not benefit from keywords until they're part of more places, e.g. the script editor auto completion (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10380 ).\r\n\r\nFeel free to bikeshed, or add any suggestions you can think of (*especially* if they come from personal experience).\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14823*\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105959/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105959/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}